    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Carbon budget estimation",
    "problem": "The existence of multiple methods for estimating the carbon budget to limit warming results in widely differing values, creating confusion for policy-making due to varying treatments of non-CO2 gases, scenario assumptions, and model frameworks.",
    "method": "The paper proposes a conceptual framework that defines and compares three carbon budget types\u2014CO2-only, Threshold Exceedance Budgets (TEBs), and Threshold Avoidance Budgets (TABs)\u2014to unravel the differences between various estimates and identify the most appropriate approach for real-world climate policy.",
    "task": "The task is to review and compare different methods for estimating carbon budgets compatible with a specific temperature limit, and to discuss and unravel the underlying reasons for the differences between the resulting estimates.",
